[
  {
    "pkheadingid": 968,
    "bookid": 65,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Definition",
    "headingPosition": 1,
    "headingid": 733,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 139407,
        "bookId": 65,
        "chapterId": 263,
        "headingId": 733,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Masson tumour is a benign vascular lesion composed of endothelial proliferation, usually within the blood vessel.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-03-31T15:07:22"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 969,
    "bookid": 65,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-O coding",
    "headingPosition": 2,
    "headingid": 734,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 139408,
        "bookId": 65,
        "chapterId": 263,
        "headingId": 734,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>None</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-03-31T15:07:22"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 970,
    "bookid": 65,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-11 coding",
    "headingPosition": 3,
    "headingid": 735,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 139409,
        "bookId": 65,
        "chapterId": 263,
        "headingId": 735,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>2F2Y Other specified benign cutaneous neoplasms</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-03-31T15:07:22"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 971,
    "bookid": 65,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Related terminology",
    "headingPosition": 4,
    "headingid": 736,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 139410,
        "bookId": 65,
        "chapterId": 263,
        "headingId": 736,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p><em>Acceptable:</em> intravascular papillary endothelial hyperplasia.</p>\r\n<p><em>Not recommended:</em> intravascular angiomatosis; vegetant intravascular haemangioendothelioma.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-03-31T15:07:22"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 972,
    "bookid": 65,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Subtype(s)",
    "headingPosition": 5,
    "headingid": 737,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 139411,
        "bookId": 65,
        "chapterId": 263,
        "headingId": 737,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Primary (pure) Masson tumour; secondary (mixed) Masson tumour; extravascular Masson tumour</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-03-31T15:07:22"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 973,
    "bookid": 65,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Localization",
    "headingPosition": 6,
    "headingid": 738,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 139412,
        "bookId": 65,
        "chapterId": 263,
        "headingId": 738,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Masson tumour rarely affects periocular tissues. The eyelids are most commonly involved, followed by the orbit and conjunctiva {34615394}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-03-31T15:07:22"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 974,
    "bookid": 65,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Clinical features",
    "headingPosition": 7,
    "headingid": 739,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 139413,
        "bookId": 65,
        "chapterId": 263,
        "headingId": 739,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Eyelid and conjunctival lesions usually present as a painless, slow-growing, solid or cystic, red-purple vascular mass {34615394}. Orbital lesions may present with proptosis.</p>\r\n<h5>Imaging</h5>\r\n<p>MRI demonstrates a well-circumscribed homogeneously enhancing mass, which is isointense on T1-weighted imaging and hyperintense on T2-weighted imaging {31903303}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-03-31T15:07:22"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 975,
    "bookid": 65,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Epidemiology",
    "headingPosition": 8,
    "headingid": 740,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 139414,
        "bookId": 65,
        "chapterId": 263,
        "headingId": 740,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>It is estimated that Masson tumour accounts for approximately 2% of all benign and malignant vascular tumours of the skin and subcutaneous tissues {22974134}. This lesion has no clear sex, age, or race predilection. There is a wide age distribution, ranging from 9&nbsp;months to 80&nbsp;years {22974134;34615394}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-03-31T15:07:22"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 976,
    "bookid": 65,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Etiology",
    "headingPosition": 9,
    "headingid": 741,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 139415,
        "bookId": 65,
        "chapterId": 263,
        "headingId": 741,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Masson tumour is currently believed to be a reactive lesion, associated with organized thrombus formation and recanalization within a dilated vascular space, pre-existing vascular abnormality, or haematoma {24294378}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-03-31T15:07:23"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 977,
    "bookid": 65,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Pathogenesis",
    "headingPosition": 10,
    "headingid": 742,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 139416,
        "bookId": 65,
        "chapterId": 263,
        "headingId": 742,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Vascular proliferation may be driven by thrombus-induced hypoxia, as supported by the upregulation of HIF1&alpha; and VEGF expression in the proliferating vascular endothelium {24294378;27323848}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-03-31T15:07:23"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 984,
    "bookid": 65,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Macroscopic appearance",
    "headingPosition": 11,
    "headingid": 749,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 139417,
        "bookId": 65,
        "chapterId": 263,
        "headingId": 749,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>The lesion appears grossly as a circumscribed red-purple mass with a cystic component.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-03-31T15:07:23"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 978,
    "bookid": 65,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Histopathology",
    "headingPosition": 12,
    "headingid": 743,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 139418,
        "bookId": 65,
        "chapterId": 263,
        "headingId": 743,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Masson tumour is a circumscribed lesion composed of papillary, interconnecting fibrous trabeculae lined by a single layer of flattened or plump endothelial cells in a background of fibrin thrombi. Primary lesions are observed within a dilated normal vascular channel, most frequently a vein. Secondary lesions arise as focal changes in the setting of a pre-existing vascular abnormality, such as a vascular malformation. A third, rare, subtype appears as an extravascular papillary endothelial proliferation in an organizing haematoma {34615394;6666836}.</p>\r\n<p>Immunohistochemistry (generally not required for diagnosis) demonstrates positivity of lesional cells for CD31, CD34, ERG, and SMA {35297528}.</p>\r\n<h5>Differential diagnosis</h5>\r\n<p>An absence of infiltrative margins, significant nuclear atypia, frequent mitotic figures, and necrosis help distinguish Masson tumour from angiosarcoma {31903303;947306;6685471}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-03-31T15:07:23"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 979,
    "bookid": 65,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Cytology",
    "headingPosition": 13,
    "headingid": 744,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 139419,
        "bookId": 65,
        "chapterId": 263,
        "headingId": 744,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-03-31T15:07:23"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 980,
